 # [Fireflies Meeting AI Clone](https://fireflies-meeting-ai-clone.vercel.app)

A full-stack meeting intelligence workspace inspired by the Fireflies.ai experience.

The application is designed to help users record meetings, manage a persistent meeting library, view interactive transcripts, generate summaries and action items, store notes, and ask an AI assistant questions about meeting content.

---

## Overview

This project recreates the core meeting-management and post-meeting workflow of a modern meeting assistant.

The application includes:

- Meeting library and dashboard
- Meeting creation and management
- Live microphone recording
- Audio playback
- Interactive transcripts
- Speaker labels and timestamps
- Transcript search
- Transcript-to-audio seeking
- AI-generated summaries
- Topics and decisions
- Action-item extraction
- Persistent notes
- Tasks
- AskFred AI meeting assistant
- Optional OpenAI integration
- Multilingual transcription support
- Light and dark themes
- Profile and Settings
- Notifications
- Windows desktop application through Electron
- SQLite persistence

---

# Features

## 1. Home Dashboard

The Home dashboard provides a Fireflies-inspired workspace for accessing meetings and meeting intelligence.

### Includes

- Recent meetings
- Meeting statistics
- Quick actions
- Record a meeting
- Upload a recording
- AskFred
- Take Notes
- Meeting navigation
- Profile menu
- Notifications

---

# 2. Meetings Library

The Meetings section stores previously created meetings.

### Meeting information

Each meeting can contain:

- Title
- Date
- Duration
- Participants
- Tags
- Transcript
- Summary
- Topics
- Decisions
- Action items
- Recording

### Library functionality

- Search meetings
- Sort meetings
- Open meetings
- Open the complete transcript
- Delete meetings directly from the library
- Create new meetings
- View previous meetings

---

# 3. Meeting Detail View

Opening a meeting provides a dedicated workspace for its content.

### Available sections

- Overview
- Transcript
- Tasks
- Notes
- AI meeting intelligence

---

# 4. Interactive Transcript

The transcript interface supports timestamped meeting conversations.

### Features

- Speaker labels
- Timestamps
- Search within transcript
- Highlighted search matches
- Click a transcript line to seek the recording
- Audio playback
- Synchronized transcript navigation

The application can work with:

- Imported transcript files
- Seeded transcript data
- Browser speech recognition when supported
- Local Whisper transcription
- Optional OpenAI transcription

---

# 5. Recording

The Windows application supports microphone recording using the browser/Electron media APIs.

### Recording workflow

1. Start a meeting
2. Grant microphone permission
3. Record audio
4. Pause/resume recording
5. Stop and save
6. Store the recording
7. Generate or attach transcript data
8. Open the saved meeting

Recordings are stored in the application's user-data directory rather than inside the source repository.

---

# 6. Audio Playback

Saved meetings can contain an audio recording.

The meeting page provides a native audio player with:

- Play/pause
- Seek bar
- Current playback position
- Duration
- Transcript synchronization

Clicking a transcript segment can move playback to the corresponding timestamp.

---

# 7. Multilingual Transcription

The application supports multiple transcription languages.

Supported behavior depends on the transcription engine being used.

### Transcription options

- Browser Speech Recognition when available
- Local Whisper transcription
- Optional OpenAI transcription

The selected transcription language can be configured from Settings.

---

# 8. AskFred AI Assistant

AskFred is the meeting-aware AI assistant.

It can be used to ask questions about saved meeting information.

### Example questions

```text
What decisions were made in this meeting?

What are the open action items?

Who is responsible for the next steps?

Summarize the main discussion.

What risks were mentioned?

What should I follow up on?
```

AskFred is designed to use meeting context rather than generating unrelated responses.

---

# 9. AI Configuration

The application supports two AI modes.

## Without an API key

The application uses grounded meeting-memory retrieval and deterministic meeting intelligence.

This allows the application to remain usable without external AI credentials.

## With an OpenAI API key

An OpenAI API key can be configured through:

```text
Profile
→ Settings
→ Meeting AI
```

When configured, OpenAI can be used for stronger:

- AskFred responses
- Meeting summaries
- Meeting analysis
- Note summaries
- Transcript processing

The API key should never be committed to GitHub.

---

# 10. Notes

The application includes a dedicated Notes workspace.

### Notes functionality

- Create notes
- Edit notes
- Save notes
- Delete notes
- Persist notes
- Associate notes with meetings where applicable
- Summarize notes with AI

Notes are stored separately from the meeting transcript so they can also be used as standalone workspace content.

---

# 11. Tasks and Action Items

Meeting action items can be converted into persistent tasks.

### Task functionality

- Create tasks
- Assign owners
- Add due dates
- Mark tasks as completed
- Delete tasks
- View meeting-related tasks

---

# 12. Notifications

The application includes a notification panel for workspace events.

Users can:

- View notifications
- Clear notifications
- Close the notification panel

---

# 13. Profile

Clicking the profile icon opens the profile menu.

The profile menu provides:

- User name
- User email
- Settings access

Settings are intentionally accessed through the profile menu rather than through a separate control-center interface.

---

# 14. Settings

The Settings section provides application configuration.

### Includes

- Appearance
- Light mode
- Dark mode
- Transcription language
- Meeting preferences
- AI configuration
- OpenAI API key configuration
- Permission-related options

---

# 15. Meeting CRUD

Meetings support full CRUD workflows.

### Create

A meeting can be created through:

- Meeting form
- Transcript import
- Recording workflow
- Uploaded audio/video

### Read

Users can:

- Browse meetings
- Open meetings
- View transcripts
- View summaries
- View tasks
- View notes
- Listen to recordings

### Update

Meeting metadata can be edited, including:

- Title
- Participants
- Related content

### Delete

Meetings can be deleted directly from the Meetings library.

---

# 16. Meeting Export / Download

A meeting can be downloaded from the meeting interface.

When available, exported meeting data can contain:

- Meeting metadata
- Transcript
- Summary
- Topics
- Decisions
- Action items
- Notes
- Recording

The exported content depends on what is available for that meeting.

---

