---

# Security

Never commit credentials or secrets to the repository.

The repository should only contain examples such as:

```text
.env.example
```

Real API keys should be stored locally or through deployment environment variables.

---

# Scope and Assumptions

This project focuses on the meeting-management and post-meeting intelligence workflow.

The assignment allows seeded, mocked, or LLM-generated meeting intelligence rather than requiring production-grade real-time speech-to-text.

Therefore the implementation supports:

- Seeded meetings
- Imported transcript data
- Browser speech recognition when available
- Local Whisper transcription
- Optional OpenAI-powered transcription and analysis

The following features are outside the primary project scope:

- Production-grade authentication
- Real-time Zoom/Google Meet bot joining
- CRM integrations
- Enterprise team collaboration
- Production multi-user authorization

These areas can be added in future versions.

---

